   "textKind": "explain",
   "content": "**Women are at least half of researchers in 23 countries**, using each country’s latest reported headcount share from **2019–2024**. Myanmar has the highest share at **76.5%**, followed by Kyrgyzstan (**61.4%**) and Azerbaijan (**60.6%**).\n\nThe countries highlighted on the map are:\n- **Europe and Central Asia:** Albania, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Bosnia and Herzegovina, Georgia, Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Moldova, Montenegro, North Macedonia and Serbia.\n- **Other parts of Asia:** Mongolia, Myanmar, the Philippines and Kuwait.\n- **Africa:** Algeria, Lesotho and Tunisia.\n- **Latin America:** Argentina, Cuba, Paraguay, Uruguay and Venezuela.\n\nRecent data cover 107 countries; unshaded countries either fall below half or lack recent data.",
